// Parser-dump driver for the parser differential test: assemble kfront (the parser) + kprint (the AST
// printer) into a standalone binary via the SELF-HOSTED compiler (kcc), Fledge-free. kprint.kite carries
// the `main` that reads /tmp/kparse_input.kite, parses it, and prints the AST — matching the OCaml
// oracle's `parse` output byte-for-byte. (Fledge can no longer build this since the compiler moved to
// method-call syntax, so run-parser-tests.sh builds it with kcc instead.) kprint's main reads the source
// path from argv, so the harness passes the file as an argument — no shared /tmp.
import "compiler/frontend/kfront.kite"
import "compiler/frontend/kprint.kite"
